title AMUS0 — Constel naming law: fake piers that can never be a real ship
prompt Keaton set the recursion loop on the 1024-round itinerary and the six-season double-seat: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve design rounds, make progress, send often, stop at custody gates.
think Read the two road-ahead docs and the REMEMBER custody gates. Season A's two seated journeys — HUNK (open image, ~90 witnesses) and CAUM (Mikrophone firmware, CAUM0-16) — both stand whole and GREEN; ran tools/caum_witness.rish GREEN to confirm.
think CAUM is genuinely complete: verify (git fsck, CAUM16) is the right capstone, and a history/log rung would VIOLATE the device's founding promise (what forgets, protects) by keeping a past the keeper never chose to keep. So the next lap is not another CAUM rung.
think The remaining Season A device-hardware rungs (Grainphone e-ink panel, cameras, refurb parts) are custody-gated (#2) and web-search-deferred, not agent-doable now. The seated ROADMAP/TASKS lag the living edge; the actual road is the two design docs handed in.
think Lindy-first crux-first over the whole road: the six-season doc explicitly RESERVES one self-approved round — the Constel test-network naming law (fake-pier dev constellations, elder Urbit fake-galaxy ancestor). It is the crux that opens local multi-pier testing of the whole Comlink/Pond/Mycelium network, and it is pure, bounded, siloed, no gate.
think Drew the waymark for the ladder: input_name constel-test-network-fake-pier-local-constellations -> AMUS (no collision, GREEN). Seated AMUS in the derive script (seated-draws comment + exclude regex) and both waymark-ladders rule twins (.claude + .cursor). waymark_derive_witness GREEN after.
think Found and resolved the source's own tension: the doc says consonants-only Hebrew-style yet lists vowel-bearing family names (queyqwinqkri, maicmalammurr). Those are the poetic Twilight-theme names, a different silo; Constel dev-net names proper are consonants-only. That keeps the safety predicate one clean scan.
obs The load-bearing safety invariant, chosen for provability: every one of Urbit's 512 real syllables carries exactly one vowel and y never appears; so a vowel-free name can never be assembled from real syllables and can never parse as a real @p. One bounded pass, fails closed — stronger and simpler than the placeholder-ship-names length trick.
obs constel/name.rye seats it: check_ship / is_valid_ship (bounded, consonant-and-digit alphabet, vowel-free), never_a_ship (the safety statement positive), check_constellation (hyphen-joined bounded run of fake piers), generate (deterministic vowel-free name per u32 index, xn silo prefix + base-21 over the palette). Named errors: VowelPresent, NameTooLong, BadCharacter, BadSegment, IndexOutOfRange. Opening triad, >=2 asserts/fn, no @memcpy, usize-free.
obs Witness proves on metal: lawful names accepted; every real @p example (zod, sarlev, sampel, palnet, sampel-palnet) refused VowelPresent by name; bound/alphabet refusing empty/long/stray/empty-segment each by name; a lawful constellation accepted; 512 generated names deterministic, collision-free, every one vowel-free by construction; over-index refused.
obs Scope held to the naming law + name primitive only. The fake-pier harness (local piers meeting over Comlink) crosses the Comlink seam and stays its own later AMUS round — named honestly, not started.
loom witness=amus_name_witness names_swept=512 collisions=0 wall_ms_note=selftest under a second after build
